WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.269 --> 00:00:18.060
When Persian regained consciousness, he was lying in bed, and Raoul was nearby, asleep on a sofa.

2
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:24.144
An angel and a devil—Christine and Erik—were watching over them.

3
00:00:24.784 --> 00:00:28.467
The Persian raised himself on one elbow and looked around the room.

4
00:00:29.227 --> 00:00:30.128
"Where are we?"

5
00:00:30.744 --> 00:00:35.048
"You're in Christine's room in my house," Erik replied.

6
00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:37.049
"As is the viscount.

7
00:00:37.650 --> 00:00:42.814
He woke up long before we knew if you were still alive, but we must let him sleep

8
00:00:42.914 --> 00:00:48.879
now. Soon I will take you up to the surface of the earth to please my wife."

9
00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:56.765
The Persian was startled by those last words, but they had no effect on Christine, who sat quietly

10
00:00:56.845 --> 00:01:03.405
reading. Erik gave the Persian something to drink and warned him not to speak to Christine or Raoul.

11
00:01:04.226 --> 00:01:09.108
The next thing the Persian knew, he was waking up in his own bed at home.

12
00:01:09.128 --> 00:01:12.829
"How did I get here?"

13
00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:17.671
the Persian asked his servant, Darius, who was standing by the bed.

14
00:01:17.691 --> 00:01:21.853
"Someone rang the doorbell last night, sir," Darius said.

15
00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:26.315
"When I answered the door, you were the only person there, and you were unconscious."

16
00:01:27.015 --> 00:01:32.005
Hoping that Raoul had also been brought home, the Persian sent a message to his house.

17
00:01:32.666 --> 00:01:39.209
But the reply that came back was upsetting: Raoul was missing, and his brother, Philippe, was dead.

18
00:01:39.809 --> 00:01:44.892
The count's body had been found on the edge of the lake underneath the opera house.

19
00:01:44.912 --> 00:01:46.733
"How terrible!"

20
00:01:47.413 --> 00:01:49.735
the Persian muttered, rereading the note.

21
00:01:50.395 --> 00:01:56.278
From what he knew about Erik and things Raoul had told him, he pieced together what had happened.

22
00:01:56.918 --> 00:02:01.017
When Philippe thought Christine and Raoul had eloped, he went after them.

23
00:02:03.299 --> 00:02:09.744
Failing to find them, Philippe had dashed back into the opera house and entered the cellars, where he

24
00:02:09.804 --> 00:02:11.586
became the siren's victim.

25
00:02:12.366 --> 00:02:16.830
The Persian shuddered, remembering Erik's playing of the funeral mass.

26
00:02:17.651 --> 00:02:18.972
He rang for his servant.

27
00:02:18.992 --> 00:02:22.315
"Darius, help me get dressed, and then summon a cab.

28
00:02:22.935 --> 00:02:24.496
I must go to the police at once."

29
00:02:25.237 --> 00:02:28.680
But the police did not take the Persian's evidence seriously.

30
00:02:29.288 --> 00:02:33.652
A murderer and kidnapper was living by the lake under the opera house?

31
00:02:34.492 --> 00:02:35.693
How was that possible?

32
00:02:36.594 --> 00:02:42.719
And so the Persian returned home, determined to write down his story and hand it to the newspapers.

33
00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:48.784
While he was writing, a mysterious man appeared at his apartment, demanding to see him.

34
00:02:48.804 --> 00:02:54.929
"The stranger won't tell me his name or show his face," Darius reported to the Persian.

35
00:02:54.949 --> 00:02:58.492
"He refuses to leave until he has spoken to you."

36
00:03:01.308 --> 00:03:04.270
"Send him in," the Persian said to his servant.

37
00:03:05.071 --> 00:03:06.171
"I know who it is."

38
00:03:07.072 --> 00:03:11.615
The Persian rose to his feet as Erik entered his drawing room.

39
00:03:12.436 --> 00:03:18.059
Erik looked extremely weak and leaned against the wall as if he was afraid of falling.

40
00:03:18.079 --> 00:03:23.183
"Murderer of Count Philippe, what have you done with Raoul and Christine?"

41
00:03:23.763 --> 00:03:25.004
the Persian demanded.

42
00:03:25.925 --> 00:03:30.328
Erik staggered under this direct attack and dragged himself to a chair.

43
00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.561
"Don't talk to me about Philippe.

44
00:03:33.081 --> 00:03:37.825
The siren caused him to have an unfortunate accident, and he fell into the lake."

45
00:03:38.525 --> 00:03:40.847
"Liar!" the Persian shouted.

46
00:03:41.827 --> 00:03:42.928
Erik bowed his head.

47
00:03:42.948 --> 00:03:49.292
"I haven't come here to talk about Philippe, but to tell you that I'm dying.

48
00:03:50.213 --> 00:03:53.235
I'm—" "Where are Christine and Raoul?"

49
00:03:53.995 --> 00:03:58.538
Erik ignored the Persian's question and went on, gasping for breath.

50
00:04:01.248 --> 00:04:02.389
"I'm dying of love.

51
00:04:03.209 --> 00:04:07.351
I've always loved Christine, and I love her now more than ever.

52
00:04:09.672 --> 00:04:13.334
You should have heard how she begged me to release you and Raoul.

53
00:04:14.174 --> 00:04:19.216
She promised to marry me if I spared your lives, so I carried you here."

54
00:04:19.236 --> 00:04:20.817
"Answer me!"

55
00:04:21.337 --> 00:04:22.518
the Persian shouted.

56
00:04:22.538 --> 00:04:25.299
"Are Christine and Raoul alive?"

57
00:04:25.319 --> 00:04:27.040
"Of course they are.

58
00:04:27.844 --> 00:04:32.185
After I took you home, I chained Raoul in a dungeon under the opera house.

59
00:04:33.005 --> 00:04:37.207
And then Erik was momentarily overcome with emotion.

60
00:04:37.227 --> 00:04:41.628
"And then Christine let me kiss her on the forehead!

61
00:04:42.368 --> 00:04:44.709
You can't imagine what that was like for me.

62
00:04:45.549 --> 00:04:48.970
My poor, unhappy mother would never let me kiss her.

63
00:04:49.610 --> 00:04:52.711
She used to toss me my mask and run away.

64
00:04:53.551 --> 00:04:56.692
Nor has any other woman ever allowed me to kiss her.

65
00:04:57.352 --> 00:05:01.895
I was so happy that I cried and fell at Christine's feet.

66
00:05:02.955 --> 00:05:06.677
And when I looked up, Christine was crying too!"

67
00:05:09.579 --> 00:05:14.441
As the Persian watched Erik sob, tears of pity came to his own eyes.

68
00:05:14.461 --> 00:05:22.325
"He's committed some terrible crimes," the Persian thought, "but what a sad, unfortunate man."

69
00:05:23.266 --> 00:05:25.607
Erik took a deep breath and began again.

70
00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:36.185
"When I felt Christine's tears on my forehead, I removed my mask so I wouldn't lose a single

71
00:05:36.385 --> 00:05:37.506
one of her tears.

72
00:05:38.166 --> 00:05:39.467
And she didn't run away!

73
00:05:40.167 --> 00:05:45.370
She stayed with me, weeping over me, weeping with me.

74
00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:51.473
At that moment I felt all the happiness the world had to offer."

75
00:05:52.394 --> 00:05:54.435
Erik began coughing and sputtering.

76
00:05:58.160 --> 00:06:02.381
"I heard Christine say, 'Poor, unhappy Erik!'

77
00:06:03.202 --> 00:06:04.262
and she took my hand.

78
00:06:05.102 --> 00:06:09.463
I had found the gold ring that she'd lost after I'd given it to her.

79
00:06:10.524 --> 00:06:16.265
I slipped the ring on her hand and told her to take it for herself and for Raoul.

80
00:06:18.986 --> 00:06:25.428
When she asked what I meant, I told her I was releasing her from her promise to marry

81
00:06:25.488 --> 00:06:31.706
me. She could marry Raoul whenever she wanted because she had cried with me."

82
00:06:32.667 --> 00:06:36.168
At that point Erik told the Persian not to look at him.

83
00:06:36.188 --> 00:06:40.970
"I have to remove my mask because I'm choking."

84
00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:44.632
The Persian walked over to the window and opened it.

85
00:06:45.332 --> 00:06:50.374
His heart was full of pity, but he kept his eyes on the scene outside his window.

86
00:06:51.074 --> 00:07:00.005
When he heard Erik take a deep breath and put the mask back on, he turned around and

87
00:07:00.105 --> 00:07:02.286
found Erik ready to continue talking.

88
00:07:02.306 --> 00:07:08.771
"I immediately brought Raoul to Christine, and they kissed in front of me.

89
00:07:09.511 --> 00:07:16.056
I made Christine promise to wear my ring until she learned of my death, when she should go

90
00:07:16.116 --> 00:07:19.618
to my house and bury the ring with my body.

91
00:07:20.219 --> 00:07:24.061
Then Christine kissed me right here!"

92
00:07:26.403 --> 00:07:27.784
Erik tapped his forehead.

93
00:07:28.628 --> 00:07:40.476
"She and Raoul hurried off together, making plans for their wedding, and leaving me—the only person still crying—alone."

94
00:07:41.497 --> 00:07:47.781
The Persian was no longer worried about Christine and Raoul because he had no doubt that Erik was

95
00:07:47.841 --> 00:07:48.621
telling the truth.

96
00:07:49.602 --> 00:07:53.425
He had no further questions for Erik, who rose to leave.

97
00:07:53.445 --> 00:07:58.028
"I do have one final request," Erik said at the door.

98
00:07:58.756 --> 00:08:02.540
"When I feel the end is near, I will notify you.

99
00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:08.845
Then you must put an ad in the newspaper so the young couple will know that I have

100
00:08:08.905 --> 00:08:17.433
died." Three weeks later an ad appeared in one of the Paris newspapers: "Erik is dead."
